  "activation_boundary": "Build only from fingerprint-locked known d1 initial scenes. Recompile the full d2b.2 resource bundle; preserve that bundle's v4 contract-only state; create explicit v5 execution identity and per-ship persisted controls. The bundle fingerprint is lineage, not an authorization signature.",
  "step_order": [
    "Opening damage-control directives, lifecycle refresh/exit and weapon boundary retain existing order.",
    "Select/persist directional command; recompute automatic linear brake from current body velocity; reject dynamic reversal.",
    "Commit engine opening boundary, aggregate per-actuator runtime uses with actual output, then integrate the interval and commit instance fuel/hull/motion.",
    "Advance projectiles using real motion endpoints; commit impact, continuous/secondary damage, personnel and lifecycle/exit changes.",
    "Resolve closing weapon boundary, then commit n+1 engine transitions; preserve all non-propulsion events.",
    "Recompile resulting runtime, validate complete engine boundary replay and persist exact v5 state. Closing output never retroactively affects the completed interval."
  ],
  "boundary_record_rationale": "The unchanged d1 kernel may change ready/running, target or response anchor on a command without producing a native lifecycle event. New step v4 records complete before/command/after/native-events for every changed engine boundary. Exact capability replay validates the chain; no fake startup event is emitted and old v3 result semantics remain unchanged.",
  "persistence_boundary": "Save only explicit v5 scene and content hash. Reload requires original known d1 source, source bindings, resource root and exact safety profile; it rebuilds resources and all static/runtime caches. Context validates resource/ship identity, persisted governor commands, supported safety state and exact timing anchors. No serialized cache token is accepted and no arbitrary old save is migrated.",
  "delivery_boundary": "Runtime unavailability and partial fuel retain d2b.3 semantics. Falling, exited and uncommanded lifecycle gates explicitly suppress physical delivery; engine time identities and transitions remain auditable instead of inventing hard-trip/reset states. Nonoperational ships reject explicit controls.",
  "differences_explained": [
    "Resource bundle, scene version, persisted control and execution lineage intentionally change serialization.",
    "Legacy forward=0.1 is 10% continuous output; named migration requests dead_slow=2%. Legacy wheel=+/-0.05 is target-turn semantics, not physically equivalent to new yaw=5% output.",
    "Known initial engines are warm ready at zero output but still require discrete response; first new force is zero and the conventional first ship reaches 4000 N forward output in the 12-step matrix.",
    "Per-case numerical fuel and motion deltas are recorded in evidence.matrix.differences, not attributed solely to response delay.",
    "Original benchmark seed projectiles are far from hulls; the 12-step matrix contains no impacts. A separate near-hull test proves impact-to-next-step runtime feedback and post-impact reload equivalence; later hit outcomes are not claimed equivalent."
  ],
